From 057a35610f69d6efa60ac808605809a52b2489a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:28:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: stream: Don't release HopIDs that were never
 allocated

tbstream_dev_attach_stream() allocates the HopIDs a stream was
configured with but ignores the result. If an allocation fails (for
example because another user of the XDomain already holds that HopID)
sdev keeps the HopID, and tbstream_dev_release() or
tbstream_dev_detach_stream() later frees an ID this stream does not
own: either another user's HopID, or one that is not allocated at all.

Similarly, tbstream_dev_alloc_in/out_hopid() release the previous HopID
before allocating the new one, but leave it in sdev if the allocation
fails, so it can be released a second time.

On a Mac Pro 6,1, after its host router had stopped answering config
requests during a stream test and the XDomain connection came back,
removing the stream's configfs directory warned twice:

  WARNING: lib/idr.c:594 at ida_free+0xe3/0x140, CPU#8: rmdir/16835
  Call Trace:
   tbstream_dev_release+0x6f/0xa0 [thunderbolt_stream]
   tbstream_dev_item_release+0x54/0x80 [thunderbolt_stream]
   config_item_cleanup+0x52/0xb0 [configfs]
   configfs_rmdir+0x344/0x3d0 [configfs]

and the same from tbstream_dev_release+0x89. The paths above are how we
read the code; the warning was not reproduced on purpose.

Forget HopIDs that could not be allocated when the stream attaches,
with a warning, and clear the previous HopID as soon as it is released.

Fixes: 6db21d817b43 ("thunderbolt: Add support for USB4STREAM")
---

Notes:
    Testing: compile-tested on this base (W=1, no new sparse warnings).  Not
    run on hardware: I didn't want to provoke HopID conflicts on the hosts I
    have, as getting there involves wedging a host router.  Instead the
    HopID functions of stream.c (tbstream_dev_release(),
    tbstream_dev_alloc_in/out_hopid(), tbstream_dev_attach_stream() and
    tbstream_dev_detach_stream()) were compiled unchanged in userspace
    against a model of the XDomain HopID IDAs, and driven through attach,
    HopID changes, detach and release with allocations that fail or find
    the HopID taken.  Before this patch, five of six scenarios free a HopID
    the stream doesn't hold (ida_free() of an unallocated ID, or another
    user's ID); after it none do and nothing is left allocated.
    
    Open question: when an allocation fails on attach the configured HopID
    is now forgotten (reads back as 0) rather than kept for a later attach.
    Keeping it would need a separate "allocated" flag; I went for the
    smaller change.
    
    How this was made: an AI coding assistant (Claude, in Claude Code) found
    the cause by reading the code after the warning, and wrote the patch,
    the userspace test and this message at my direction.

 drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
index fe88341c4e29..868082a25728 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
@@ -1337,8 +1337,10 @@ static int tbstream_dev_alloc_in_hopid(struct tbstream_dev *sdev, int hopid)
 	struct tb_xdomain *xd = tbstream_dev_xdomain(sdev);
 	int ret;
 
-	if (sdev->in_hopid > 0 && sdev->in_hopid != hopid)
+	if (sdev->in_hopid > 0 && sdev->in_hopid != hopid) {
 		tb_xdomain_release_in_hopid(xd, sdev->in_hopid);
+		sdev->in_hopid = 0;
+	}
 	if (!hopid) {
 		sdev->in_hopid = hopid;
 		return 0;
@@ -1363,8 +1365,10 @@ static int tbstream_dev_alloc_out_hopid(struct tbstream_dev *sdev, int hopid)
 	struct tb_xdomain *xd = tbstream_dev_xdomain(sdev);
 	int ret;
 
-	if (sdev->out_hopid > 0 && sdev->out_hopid != hopid)
+	if (sdev->out_hopid > 0 && sdev->out_hopid != hopid) {
 		tb_xdomain_release_out_hopid(xd, sdev->out_hopid);
+		sdev->out_hopid = 0;
+	}
 	if (!hopid) {
 		sdev->out_hopid = hopid;
 		return 0;
@@ -1584,10 +1588,22 @@ tbstream_dev_attach_stream(struct tbstream_dev *sdev, struct tbstream_group *sg)
 		if (sdev->in_hopid <= 0 && sdev->out_hopid <= 0)
 			service_get_hopids(stream->svc, name, &sdev->in_hopid,
 					   &sdev->out_hopid);
-		if (sdev->in_hopid)
-			tbstream_dev_alloc_in_hopid(sdev, sdev->in_hopid);
-		if (sdev->out_hopid)
-			tbstream_dev_alloc_out_hopid(sdev, sdev->out_hopid);
+		/*
+		 * None of these are allocated yet. Forget the ones that
+		 * can't be so they are not released later.
+		 */
+		if (sdev->in_hopid &&
+		    tbstream_dev_alloc_in_hopid(sdev, sdev->in_hopid)) {
+			pr_warn("%s: in HopID %d not available\n", name,
+				sdev->in_hopid);
+			sdev->in_hopid = 0;
+		}
+		if (sdev->out_hopid &&
+		    tbstream_dev_alloc_out_hopid(sdev, sdev->out_hopid)) {
+			pr_warn("%s: out HopID %d not available\n", name,
+				sdev->out_hopid);
+			sdev->out_hopid = 0;
+		}
 	}
 
 	service_update_properties(stream->svc, name, sdev->in_hopid,

base-commit: a93a8e3200002f0c345fec4c340390e9a60aabc7
